# Evaluation reports are machine output: one JSON document per run, holding the
# provider's answer for every case. They are committed because this corpus is
# synthetic and content-free, so a later change can re-derive a comparison from
# them instead of paying for fresh provider calls — see
# packages/agent-harness/evals/semantic-trigger/README.md. Nobody reads them as a
# diff, and left unmarked they bury a pull request's real changes under hundreds
# of thousands of lines, so GitHub is told to collapse them by default.
packages/agent-harness/evals/*/reports/*.json linguist-generated=true
